  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development results in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. Furthermore, the applicant fails to&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;indicate that the home will be provided for children and young people who meet this threshold i.e. being a&amp;nbsp;specialist and can demonstrate experience of managing complex young people and those with disabilities,&amp;nbsp;thus would not meet the current needs of LBBD Children’s Social Care, as confirmed by LBBD&#x27;s Lead Commissioner in Children&#x27;s Social Care.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#x27;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Policiy&amp;nbsp;D7, H1, H12 and S2 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Policies SP3 and&amp;nbsp;SPDG1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
  ],
